.SH "نام (NAME)"
fvwm-menu-directory \- builds a directory browsing menu for fvwm
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
fvwm\-menu\-directory [ \fB\-\-help\fP|\fB\-h\fP|\fB\-?\fP ] [ \fB\-\-version\fP|\fB\-V\fP ]
[ \fB\-\-name\fP|\fB\-na\fP NAME ] [ \fB\-\-title\fP|\fB\-t\fP NAME ]
[ \fB\-\-item\fP|\fB\-it\fP NAME ] [ \fB\-\-icon\-title\fP|\fB\-icon\-t\fP XPM ]
[ \fB\-\-icon\-dir\fP|\fB\-icon\-d\fP XPM ] [ \fB\-\-icon\-file\fP|\fB\-icon\-f\fP XPM ]
[ \fB\-\-icon\-app\fP|\fB\-icon\-a\fP XPM ] [ \fB\-\-wm\-icons\fP ] [ \fB\-\-dir\fP|\fB\-d\fP NAME ]
[ \fB\-\-order\fP|\fB\-o\fP NUM ] [ \fB\-\-[no]all\fP|\fB\-a\fP ] [ \fB\-\-[no]links\fP|\fB\-l\fP ]
[ \fB\-\-xterm\fP|\fB\-x\fP CMD ] [ \fB\-\-exec\-title\fP|\fB\-exec\-t\fP CMD ]
[ \fB\-\-exec\-file\fP|\fB\-exec\-f\fP CMD ] [ \fB\-\-exec\-app\fP|\fB\-exec\-a\fP [CMD] ]
[ \fB\-\-command\-title\fP|\fB\-command\-t\fP CMD ] [ \fB\-\-command\-file\fP|\fB\-command\-f\fP CMD ]
[ \fB\-\-command\-app\fP|\fB\-command\-a\fP CMD ] [ \fB\-\-[no]reuse\fP|\fB\-r\fP ]
[ \fB\-\-[no]check\-subdirs\fP|\fB\-ch\fP ] [ \fB\-\-special\-dirs\fP|\fB\-s\fP [VALUE] ]
[ \fB\-\-[no]memory\-for\-speed\fP|\fB\-mem\fP ] [ \fB\-\-menu\-style\fP|\fB\-men\fP NAME ]
[ \fB\-\-func\-name\fP|\fB\-f\fP NAME ]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
A perl script which provides an output to read in with PipeRead to build
an fvwm menu containing a directory listing. Almost everything can be
configured.
.SH "HINTS"
.sp
The title item with its own attached action is usually added to the
menu. This may be used to define an action for the directory for which
the menu is built, such as starting a terminal in this directory (the
default). However, this may annoy some users. To disable the title
action use \fB\-\-command\-title ""\fP, to remove the title completely use
\fB\-\-title ""\fP.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.sp
\fB\-\-help\fP
.RS 4
Show the usage and exit.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-version\fP
.RS 4
Show version and exit.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-name\fP \fIname\fP
.RS 4
Menu name, used only with \fB\-\-reuse\fP, default is \f(CRMenuBrowser\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-title\fP \fItitle\fP
.RS 4
Menu title format, default is \f(CR\*(Aq%*\-40p\*(Aq\fP \- last 40 characters of the
current full path. TAB can be specified as \f(CR\*(Aq\(rst\*(Aq\fP, but in .fvwm2rc you
should specify a double backslash or a real TAB.
.sp
Format specifiers:
\f(CR%d\fP \- the current directory name \f(CR%p\fP \- the current directory full path.
.sp
These specifiers can receive an optional integer size, positive for
right adjusted string or negative for left adjusted, example: \f(CR%8x\fP;
and optional \f(CR*num\fP or \f(CR*\-num\fP, which means to leave only the first
or last (if minus) num of chars, the num must be greater than 3, since the
striped part is replaced with .\|.\|., example: \f(CR%*30x\fP. Both can be combined:
\f(CR%\-10*\-20x\fP, this instructs to get only the 20 last characters, but if the
length is less then 10 \- to fill with up to 10 spaces on the right.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-item\fP \fIformat\fP
.RS 4
Menu item format, default is \f(CR\*(Aq%n\*(Aq\fP. TAB and width modifiers for \f(CR%n\fP,
\f(CR%N\fP and \f(CR%s\fP can be specified as described in \fB\-\-title\fP above.
Note, specifying a non default format slows the script.
.sp
Format specifiers:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
%n \- file/dir name (without the path)
%N \- file/dir name (full with the path)
%d \- file/dir date (yyyy\-mm\-dd HH:MM:SS)
%D \- file/dir date (yyyy\-mm\-dd)
%s \- file/dir size (in bytes)
%t \- file/dir type (File|Dir |Link|Sock|Blck|Char|Pipe)
%T \- file/dir type (F|D|L|S|B|C|P)
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
Example: \f(CR\-\-title \*(Aq%*\-40p\(rstDate, Type\(rstSize\*(Aq \-\-item \*(Aq%*40n\(rst%d %t\(rst%s\*(Aq\fP
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-icon\-title\fP \fIicon\fP
.RS 4
Menu title icon, default is none.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-icon\-dir\fP \fIicon\fP
.RS 4
Menu dir icon, default is none.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-icon\-file\fP \fIicon\fP
.RS 4
Menu file icon, default is none.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-icon\-app\fP \fIicon\fP
.RS 4
Menu application icon, default is none.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-wm\-icons\fP
.RS 4
Define icon names suitable for use with wm\-icons package. Currently this
is equivalent to: \f(CR\-\-icon\-title menu/folder\-open.xpm \-\-icon\-item
menu/file.xpm \-\-icon\-dir menu/folder.xpm \-\-icon\-app menu/utility.xpm\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-dir\fP \fIdir\fP
.RS 4
Starting dir, default is \f(CR${HOME\-.}\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-order\fP \fInumber\fP
.RS 4
In the range (\-6 .. 6), default is 5:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
1 \- do not sort
2 \- dirs first
3 \- files first
4 \- sort by name
5 \- dirs first
6 \- files first
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
Negative number represents reverse order.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-[no]all\fP
.RS 4
Show hidden files, like in \*(Aqls \-A\*(Aq, default is \fB\-\-noall\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-[no]links\fP
.RS 4
Follow linked directories, default is \fB\-\-nolinks\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-xterm\fP \fIcommand\fP
.RS 4
X terminal call, default is \*(Aqxterm \-e\*(Aq.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-exec\-title\fP \fIcommand\fP
.RS 4
An fvwm Exec command on directory title (usually the shell), default is
\f(CR${SHELL\-/bin/sh}\fP. \*(Aq\-\*(Aq means no Exec command, i.e. Nop. If the command
is not started with \*(Aq^\*(Aq X terminal call is prepended. The command is
started in the currently browsed directory.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-exec\-file\fP \fIcommand\fP
.RS 4
An fvwm Exec command on regular files, default is \f(CR${EDITOR\-vi}\fP. \*(Aq\-\*(Aq
means no Exec command, i.e. Nop. If the command is not started with \*(Aq^\*(Aq
X terminal call is prepended. The actual file name is appended to the
command.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-exec\-app\fP [\fIcommand\fP]
.RS 4
An fvwm Exec command on +x files, default is \*(Aq\-\*(Aq, which means the same
command as on regular files. If no command is given, it is assumed to be
empty \- simply run the +x file. If the command is not started with \*(Aq^\*(Aq X
terminal call is prepended. The actual file name is appended to the
command.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-command\-title\fP \fIcommand\fP
.RS 4
An fvwm command to execute on title. If this option is not given (or
command is \*(Aq\-\*(Aq), the \fB\-\-exec\-title\fP is used instead. In the command,
\f(CR%d\fP is substituted with the full directory path.
.sp
In fact, \fI\-\-exec\-title=tcsh\fP is equivalent to \fI\-\-command\-title=\*(AqExec cd %d; xterm
\-e tcsh\*(Aq\fP.
.sp
The empty value disables the title action.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-command\-file\fP \fIcommand\fP
.RS 4
An fvwm command to execute on regular files. If this option is not given
(or command is \*(Aq\-\*(Aq), the \fB\-\-exec\-file\fP is used instead. In the
command, \f(CR%f\fP is substituted with the full file path.
.sp
In fact, \fI\-\-exec\-file=vi\fP is equivalent to \fI\-\-command\-file=\*(AqExec xterm \-e vi %f\*(Aq\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-command\-app\fP \fIcommand\fP
.RS 4
An fvwm command to execute on x files. If this option is not given (or
command is \*(Aq\-\*(Aq), the *\-\-command\-app* is used instead. In the command,
`%f+` is substituted with the full file path.
.sp
In fact, \fI\-\-exec\-app=^exec\fP is equivalent to \fI\-\-command\-app=\*(AqExec exec %f\*(Aq\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-[no]reuse\fP
.RS 4
No pop\-up menus, reuse the same menu, default is \fB\-\-noreuse\fP. When you
specify this option the Menu action is used, not Popup. Also, the \fB\-\-name\fP
parameter is not ignored, and \fB\-\-dir\fP parameter is ignored if there is
\f(CR~/.fvwm/.fvwm\-menu\-directory.dir\fP file. This file is only created or used
with this option specified, it is the only solution for the current fvwm
menu state.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-[no]check\-subdirs\fP
.RS 4
Check all subdirs for having execute (+x) permission and replace
"Popup"/"Menu" command with Nop for these without permissions. This has a
visual effect of disabling popup triangle in the subdirectory item. The
default is \fB\-\-nocheck\-subdirs\fP, because: 1) enabling this slows a bit the
script, 2) with this option enabled, if no icons used and no dir/file
separate sorting used there is no way to know that the item is directory
and not file.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-special\-dirs\fP \fIvalue\fP
.RS 4
Add .. or ~ or / special directories according to given optional value.
Without with option these directories are not added. Default value if
not specified is "1,2". The value is comma separated ordered special
directory indexes, where 1 is parent directory, 2 is home directory, 3
is root directory. If minus is prepended to the value, special
directories are added at the bottom of menu instead of top. Value 0 or
any bad value is equivalent to non\-specifying this option at all.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-[no]memory\-for\-speed\fP
.RS 4
Use speed optimization, i.e. use previously created directory menus
without destroying it when closed, default is \fB\-\-nomemory\-for\-speed\fP.
.sp
Warning: speed optimization takes up a lot of memory that is never freed
again while fvwm is running.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-menu\-style\fP \fIname\fP
.RS 4
Assign MenuStyle name to the menus.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-func\-name\fP \fIname\fP
.RS 4
Overwrite the default MissingSubmenuFunction name that is
FuncFvwmMenuDirectory.
.RE
.sp
Option parameters can be specified either using \*(Aq=\*(Aq or in the next
argument. Short options are ok if not ambiguous: \f(CR\-a\fP, \f(CR\-x\fP,
\f(CR\-icon\-f\fP; but be careful with short options, what is now unambiguous,
can become ambiguous in the next versions.
.SH "نحوه استفاده (USAGE)"
.sp
Put this into your fvwm configuration file to invoke the script:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
AddToFunc FuncFvwmMenuDirectory
+ I PipeRead "fvwm\-menu\-directory \-d $0"
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
More complex example:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
AddToFunc FuncFvwmMenuDirectory
+ I PipeRead "fvwm\-menu\-directory \-d \*(Aq$0\*(Aq \-x \*(AqEterm \-g 80x40 \-e\*(Aq \(rs\(rs
    \-a \-l \-o 6 \-\-exec\-app \-\-exec\-title \*(Aqtcsh \-l\*(Aq \(rs\(rs
    \-\-exec\-file \*(Aqvim \-R\*(Aq \-t \*(AqGo to: %d\*(Aq \-\-wm\-icons"
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
And put this in the menu from which you want to pop\-up the directory
menus:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
AddToMenu SomeMenu MissingSubmenuFunction FuncFvwmMenuDirectory
+ "Home Directory" Popup $[HOME]
+ "Httpd Directory" Popup /home/httpd
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
Note: please use absolute path names.
.sp
It is a good idea to set the menu pop\-up delay to something positive and
enable busy cursor
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
MenuStyle * PopupDelayed, PopupDelay 200
BusyCursor DynamicMenu True
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
in your configuration file when using this script for better results.
.sp
Another interesting usage (\f(CR\*(Aq\-\-reuse\*(Aq\fP or \f(CR\*(Aq\-r\*(Aq\fP is mandatory for this):
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
AddToMenu Browser
+ DynamicPopupAction PipeRead \(rs\(rs
  "fvwm\-menu\-directory \-r \-na Browser \-d / \-s"
AddToMenu SomeMenu "My Browser" Menu Browser
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
Here the \f(CR\*(Aq\-\-dir\*(Aq\fP parameter (starting directory) is ignored if there is
\f(CR~/.fvwm/.fvwm\-menu\-directory.dir\fP file, which you can delete.
